===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|jǫkull|lang=non}} (alternative spelling {{term|jökull|lang=non}}), diminutive of the Old Norse {{term|jaki||a piece of ice, broken ice|lang=non}}.<ref>[http://web.ff.cuni.cz/cgi-bin/uaa_slovnik/gmc_search_v3?cmd=viewthis&id=cv:b0327:35 JÖKULL] from Cleasby/Vigfusson</ref><ref name="da">[http://ordnet.dk/ddo/ordbog?query=j%C3%B8kel jøkel substantiv, fælleskøn]</ref>

